# I04.var07 prospective contract readiness — NO_GO

Date: 2026-10-08. This is a read-only feasibility decision, not a native result or package acceptance.

Proposed one-cell child of accepted I04.var03 idle-system-between v1.0.1: SystemTransfer.TFTIME 10.5 -> 19, with positive TFDT 0.5 unchanged and PDESC updated. The accepted parent has one ready aircraft at TEACH-UNIT and one at TEACH-UNIT-2 before h19; the second group mission is notified/activated at h19, requests two, starts at h20 and completes at h22. In its original model.log, system 0 transfers out at h10.5 and into TEACH-UNIT-2 at h11, and the h19 mission allocates aircraft 1 and then 0 from the target unit. The accepted report contains 4,044 cells.

Installed SIMLOX 2017 manual physical pages 225 and 480–481 specify ready-only system transfers, higher priority than missions, pending transfer checks when an aircraft becomes ready, and TFDT as transit delay. They do not specify the simultaneous h19 event-queue order or exact two-unit-group partial allocation, waiting, preassignment, and preparation diagnostics. The accepted A03 one-of-two trace shows partial allocation and a mission-waiting line; accepted A02 at-return shows a later-ready aircraft can be preassigned. Neither witnesses this transfer-arrival/group-mission combination. Accepted I04 transfer traces do not contain a same-time scheduled transfer and new group mission.

A transfer-first physical hypothesis moves system 0 into transit during [19,19.5) and leaves aircraft 1 at the target; a mission-first diagnostic could assign both aircraft before the transfer request is processed and defer transfer to post-mission readiness. Even transfer-first has at least two unsupported group behaviors: partial assignment of aircraft 1 during [19,19.5), or waiting without assignment until system 0 arrives. The h19 SystemResults NSYMA/NSYMR/NSYRY cells and possibly mission timing therefore differ. Treat mission-first as a diagnostic/NO_GO for a stronger priority claim, not as a blanket accepted successful arm. No prospective closed full-line grammar and independently derived 4,044-cell report oracle for every allowed branch has been established.

Recovery condition: obtain a source-backed, independently reviewed finite causal transcript grammar for this exact group/transfer interaction, with explicit same-time partial order, owner/ready/assigned/transit ledger, mission timing and terminal state, and a complete typed 4,044-cell report oracle per allowed branch before any new native run. Preserve this NO_GO; do not fit new alternatives after observation. No I04.var07 package, input, checker, or native run was created here.
